        "id": "ch7_2_4-1",
        "text": "WebSocket APIs\nWebSocket APIs use JSON to move data between clients and servers. Like REST APIs, they are based\non HTTP, but unlike REST APIs, WebSocket APIs also use their own protocol, called the WebSocket\nprotocol, an extension of HTTP, which allows for a wider range of operations. They are stateful and\nbi-directional; the server may initiate communication with a connected client. This makes them\nextremely powerful, but also harder to use.\nLet\u2019s take a closer look at how we can work with the most common API type \u2013 the REST API.",
